\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Sequence diagrams comparing synchronous and asynchronous communication models in cloud-native applications across Connection Per Request (CPR) and Persistent Connection Reuse (PCR). In the CPR paradigm for both gateway frameworks (Flask and FastAPI), every request made to the frontend through the backend service relies on TCP-based handshakes and tearing down the connection after the system replies to the request. In contrast to the PCR paradigm, the connection is established immediately on the first request and remains open until all HTTP/1.1 requests are processed.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline{(a)}{\ignorespaces {Synchronous Flask gateway framework}}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline{(b)}{\ignorespaces {Asynchronous FastAPI gateway framework}}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
