\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  {\fontencoding  {T1}\fontseries  {b}\selectfont  {T}he autonomic controller architectures. The controller's architecture consists of four main components, i.e., sensing, analysis, decision, and action. The controller continuously runs the process to monitor, analyze, plan, and execute actions based on specific metrics scraped from Prometheus. The action execution to patch the frontend deployments will be enforced whenever the threshold criteria are breached by a catastrophic queuing request at the frontend service. The threshold criteria are defined by an empirical mathematical calculation to predict $\lambda _{sat}$ and are combined with actual system degradation, as measured by real-time SLA monitoring ($L_{SLA}$). }  }}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ctr-arc}{{2}{5}{}{figure.2}{}}
